VI  - 137
IP  - 1
DP  - 2010 Jan
TI  - An approach to interventional pulmonary fellowship training.
PG  - 195-9
LID - 10.1378/chest.09-0494 [doi]
AB  - Interventional pulmonology continues to be a specialty that is experiencing an 
      evolution of new technologies, with an emphasis on multidisciplinary care. The 
      diversity and application of these procedures in patients with more complex 
      conditions is leading to the need for more specific recommendations in training 
      within this area. As patient safety and outcomes-based measures of clinical 
      practice and procedures are in the forefront, the need for standardization in 
      procedural training in high-volume centers of excellence beyond pulmonary and 
      critical care fellowships must be considered. Other procedure-based specialties 
      have developed such training programs, with structured curricula to enhance 
      patient safety and outcomes, develop validated metrics for competency assessment 
      of trainees, improve trainee education, and further advance the field by 
      fostering research.
