TI  - Training program of interventional pulmonology fellowships: USA.
PG  - S415-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.11.55 [doi]
AB  - Interventional pulmonary (IP) is an emerging subspecialty of pulmonary medicine 
      which focuses on procedures of the airway, lung, and pleura. As the number of 
      advance procedures increases with the growth of this field, additional formal 
      training is required to offer the full complement of techniques. IP fellowship is 
      a dedicated 12 months fellowship in the United States which occurs after 
      pulmonary/critical care fellowship. There have been several recent milestones in 
      this field which include validated exams based on didactic knowledge and 
      structural organization of fellowship organizations.
