TI  - [Technology update and field expansion of bronchoscopy interventional diagnosis 
      in 2021].
PG  - 1782-1785
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112137-20220224-00387 [doi]
AB  - In recent years, with the rapid development of interventional pulmonary diseases, 
      new instruments and new concepts are constantly updated. The increased detection 
      rate of pulmonary nodules increases the demand of patients. These factors jointly 
      promote the continuous progress of bronchoscopy diagnosis and treatment 
      technology. The following techniques including thin/ultrathin bronchoscopes, 
      radial probe endobronchial ultrasound (R-EBUS), and navigation bronchoscopy 
      including virtual navigation bronchoscopy (VNB) and electromagnetic navigation 
      bronchoscopy (ENB), robotic-assisted bronchoscopy (RAB), frozen biopsy for the 
      diagnosis of diffuse lung diseases are particularly prominent and important in 
      clinical practice. This paper reviews the progress and application of 
      bronchoscopy in interventional diagnosis through the review of literature 
      published in 2021.
